{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00943",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.6,
      "end_seconds": 6.52,
      "duration_seconds": 5.92,
      "text": "Hello, come in, come in. Is it still pouring out there? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 9.09,
      "end_seconds": 18.74,
      "duration_seconds": 9.65,
      "text": "Chucking it down. I dropped Mum at the door and then it took me twenty minutes to park. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 20.64,
      "end_seconds": 27.29,
      "duration_seconds": 6.65,
      "text": "Is this the right place? I'd like to see Dr Whitby. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 28.06,
      "end_seconds": 36.11,
      "duration_seconds": 8.05,
      "text": "I'm Dr Whitby, Mrs Lowe, and this is the right place. How are you today? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.6,
      "end_seconds": 52.27,
      "duration_seconds": 13.67,
      "text": "Oh, very well, dear, apart from the telly, someone's moved my chair, and the girl who does my tea, she's from Spain, no, Portugal, no, I can't remember. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 53.23,
      "end_seconds": 60.15,
      "duration_seconds": 6.92,
      "text": "I'm Priya, Mrs Lowe, I'm from Leicester. I come four times a day. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.34,
      "end_seconds": 64.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "That's it. Priya. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 66.29,
      "end_seconds": 76.36,
      "duration_seconds": 10.07,
      "text": "Doctor, it's the urine infections. She's had three since Christmas, and each time she gets muddled. This week she's confused again."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.44,
      "end_seconds": 81.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "How is the confusion different from her usual?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 84.17,
      "end_seconds": 96.34,
      "duration_seconds": 12.17,
      "text": "She didn't know me on Monday. She asked who I was, and then she thought it was morning when it was evening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.07,
      "end_seconds": 101.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "I knew you, Priya, I was just being silly. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.07,
      "end_seconds": 109.7,
      "duration_seconds": 5.63,
      "text": "I see. Mrs Lowe, any burning when you pass water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.44,
      "end_seconds": 117.04,
      "duration_seconds": 4.6,
      "text": "A bit of a sting, yes. Down below."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 118.2,
      "end_seconds": 124.91,
      "duration_seconds": 6.71,
      "text": "And she's going all the time, doctor. Every hour, Priya says."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 127.38,
      "end_seconds": 131.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "Every hour or so, yes. Even at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.23,
      "end_seconds": 135.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Any fever, shivering?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 137.88,
      "end_seconds": 145.04,
      "duration_seconds": 7.16,
      "text": "No, her temperature's been normal, I check it with the ear thermometer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.79,
      "end_seconds": 149.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "Any falls?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 150.54,
      "end_seconds": 153.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "No falls, thank goodness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.54,
      "end_seconds": 157.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "What medicines is she on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 160.47,
      "end_seconds": 173.23,
      "duration_seconds": 12.76,
      "text": "Trimethoprim, 100 mg, at night, to prevent the infections. Amlodipine, 5 mg, once a day. And paracetamol, 500 mg, when she needs it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.1,
      "end_seconds": 177.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "Thank you. Any conditions, Jean?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 179.21,
      "end_seconds": 183.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "Recurrent urinary infections, obviously, and high blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.54,
      "end_seconds": 191.0,
      "duration_seconds": 4.46,
      "text": "Dementia in the family, anything like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 193.46,
      "end_seconds": 196.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "Her sister had dementia, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.88,
      "end_seconds": 202.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "Who's at home with her?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 204.71,
      "end_seconds": 211.31,
      "duration_seconds": 6.6,
      "text": "She lives alone, with us coming in four times a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.0,
      "end_seconds": 218.72,
      "duration_seconds": 4.72,
      "text": "And what did she do for work?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 221.0,
      "end_seconds": 229.54,
      "duration_seconds": 8.54,
      "text": "I was a nurse, dear, for forty years. I'd know a urine infection if I saw one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.2,
      "end_seconds": 263.07,
      "duration_seconds": 15.87,
      "text": "I'm sure you would. Let me check you. Pulse 82, blood pressure 138 over 76, temperature 36.9, oxygen 96 percent, breathing 16, and weight 59 kilos."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 265.67,
      "end_seconds": 268.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "Is the temperature normal? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.5,
      "end_seconds": 287.53,
      "duration_seconds": 7.03,
      "text": "Yes. Mrs Lowe, I'm going to press gently on your tummy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 289.69,
      "end_seconds": 292.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Mind my cardigan. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.98,
      "end_seconds": 301.18,
      "duration_seconds": 6.2,
      "text": "There's tenderness just above the pubic bone, in the lower tummy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 303.86,
      "end_seconds": 307.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "Ooh, yes, that's the one. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.92,
      "end_seconds": 318.38,
      "duration_seconds": 9.46,
      "text": "Given the sting, the going every hour, and the confusion, this looks like another urine infection."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 320.94,
      "end_seconds": 323.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "Not again. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 325.04,
      "end_seconds": 333.3,
      "duration_seconds": 8.26,
      "text": "It's very common at her age. Make sure she drinks plenty of water through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 334.42,
      "end_seconds": 339.89,
      "duration_seconds": 5.47,
      "text": "I'll keep a jug by her chair. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 341.29,
      "end_seconds": 346.84,
      "duration_seconds": 5.55,
      "text": "And keep an eye on how clear her thinking is. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 349.18,
      "end_seconds": 353.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.38,
      "text": "What if it doesn't clear up? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 355.98,
      "end_seconds": 365.37,
      "duration_seconds": 9.39,
      "text": "If she's still muddled in three days, or she gets a fever, get in touch and we'll see her again."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 366.43,
      "end_seconds": 369.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "Three days. I'll ring. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 372.21,
      "end_seconds": 377.91,
      "duration_seconds": 5.7,
      "text": "Thank you, doctor. Has someone moved my chair? ~"
    }
  ]
}
